## What I changed
- **`src/money.ts`** (new) — exports `formatMoney(cents, currency)` exactly as planned: sign, thousands grouping via the `\B(?=(\d{3})+(?!\d))` regex, two-decimal fraction, currency suffix.
- **`src/invoice.ts`** — imports `formatMoney` from `./money.ts`; `formatInvoiceAmount` body is now just `return formatMoney(cents, currency)`. `invoiceTotal` and `renderInvoice` untouched (I moved the import to after the type export, so the diff to the functional code is minimal).
- **`src/receipt.ts`** — imports `formatMoney`; `formatReceiptAmount` body is now `return formatMoney(cents, currency)`. `renderReceipt` untouched.
- **`src/money.test.ts`** (new) — all six planned `formatMoney` cases.
- **`src/receipt.test.ts`** — added the refund assertion: `renderReceipt([{ name: 'refund', cents: -1250 }], 'EUR')` → `"refund -12.50 EUR\nTOTAL -12.50 EUR"`.

The refund fix works because `formatMoney` puts the sign on both the item and the total, whereas the old `formatReceiptAmount` dropped it (`-12` → `-12.50` was fine for whole euros but `-1250` → `-12.50` missing the minus).

